-- 2x2x2 cartesian deck with a deliberate zero-volume cell.
-- Used by an earlier test_pinchout_drops_zero_volume_cell.
--
-- The top z-layer (k_slot=3) is pulled down to z=1 wherever cell (1,1,1)
-- (or any cell sharing its top pillars) has a corner. Matching-Z
-- demands the change extend to ALL slots touching pillars (1,1),
-- (2,1), (1,2), (2,2) at k_slot=3 — concretely positions where
-- i_slot ∈ {1,2,3} AND j_slot ∈ {1,2,3}.
--
-- Effect on cells (per-face uniqueness rule, ):
--   cell (1,1,1)            fully collapsed — 4 faces have only 2 unique
--                            nodes → dropped as zero-volume.
--   cells (0,1,1), (1,0,1)  share TWO pillars with (1,1,1); one face
--                            collapses to 2 unique nodes → dropped.
--   cell (0,0,1)            shares ONE pillar (1,1) only → wedge whose
--                            worst face still has 3 unique → KEPT.
-- Net: 8 − 3 = 5 active+real cells after build_topology.
-- (See tests/test_unstructured.py::test_pinchout_drops_zero_volume_cell.
--  An earlier "7 cells" note here was geometrically naive — corrected
--  2026-05-24 to match the actual per-face rule.)

SPECGRID
  2 2 2 1 F /

COORD
  0 0 0  0 0 2
  1 0 0  1 0 2
  2 0 0  2 0 2
  0 1 0  0 1 2
  1 1 0  1 1 2
  2 1 0  2 1 2
  0 2 0  0 2 2
  1 2 0  1 2 2
  2 2 0  2 2 2  /

ZCORN
  16*0
  16*1
  16*1
  2 2 2 2   2 1 1 1   2 1 1 1   2 1 1 1 /

ACTNUM
  8*1 /
